'''Grasping Vines''' is a [[debuff]] that reduces the [[movement speed]] of the character. Each stack is indicated by a vine that runs from the player to the floor, with the visuals changing based on the source of the debuff. Grasping Vines are elastic and will stretch while attached to the player. Each stack of Grasping Vines additively inflicts 8% less Movement Speed, up to a hard cap of 90% less Movement Speed.<ref>https://www.pathofexile.com/forum/view-thread/3357433</ref> Most sources of Grasping Vines are capped at 10 vines (80% less Movement Speed), though different sources can stack independently.

Teleporting with any movement skill that instantly moves you (such as {{il|Flame Dash}} or {{il|Blink Arrow}}) instantly removes all stacks of the Grasping Vines debuff. Other movement skills like {{il|Leap Slam}} or {{il|Shield Charge}} will remove stacks based on the distance moved. {{il|The Stampede}} can bypass the penalty of the vines entirely.

Certain applications of Grasping Vines, such as those inflicted by [[Namharim, Born of Night]] in Harvest maps, prevent the use of movement skills.


